</figure>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly discuss how different operators
are handled in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
and defer a detailed discussion with examples to Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A More details on Algorithm 1 ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.
The scores for logical operators, negation <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\neg\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\neg\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, conjunction <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and disjunction <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\lor\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\lor\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
are computed using simple rules from probability theory.
Concretely, LogSTOP for <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\land\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of the LogSTOPs for <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l12" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), and
the LogSTOP for <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\lor\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\lor\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed using DeMorgan’s law
(line <a href="#alg1.l14" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
The score for the "next" operator <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcirc\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">○</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcirc\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by shifting the timestep by one window (line <a href="#alg1.l16" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>).
Scores for the "always" (<math id="S3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>) and "until" (<math id="S3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\mathcal{U}\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\mathcal{U}\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)
operators
are computed recursively using the scores for these properties at the next window (lines <a href="#alg1.l18" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>-<a href="#alg1.l20" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
Informally, the LogSTOP for Always <math id="S3.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed with a <span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"temporal and"</span> over <math id="S3.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and Always <math id="S3.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> at the next window, <math id="S3.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+w</annotation></semantics></math>.
Similarly, the LogSTOP for <math id="S3.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\mathbin{\mathcal{U}}\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">𝒰</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\mathbin{\mathcal{U}}\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed with a <span id="S3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"temporal or"</span> over (1) <math id="S3.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.p6.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and (2) <math id="S3.p6.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.p6.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p6.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{1}\mathbin{\mathcal{U}}\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">𝒰</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{1}\mathbin{\mathcal{U}}\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> at the next window.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Complexity analysis for LogSTOP.</span>
The computational complexity of Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 LogSTOP: An Algorithm for Computing STOPs ‣ LogSTOP: Temporal Scores over Prediction Sequences for Matching and Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
for a temporal property <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> with length <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi|</annotation></semantics></math> and a sequence of <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> predictions
is <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This uses dynamic programming to cache scores for all sub-properties over the sequence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.
The key observation here is that at any timestep <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the LogSTOP for <span id="S3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">any</span> property <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed in <math id="S3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(|\varphi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(|\varphi|)</annotation></semantics></math> given the LogSTOPs for its sub-properties at <math id="S3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and itself at <math id="S3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+w</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is because the LogSTOPs for temporal properties are defined recursively and there are at most <math id="S3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varphi|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varphi|</annotation></semantics></math> sub-properties.
For <math id="S3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T/w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T/w</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps, this results in <math id="S3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((T/w)\cdot|\varphi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((T/w)\cdot|\varphi|)</annotation></semantics></math> time.
Since the smoothing operation takes <math id="S3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(w)</annotation></semantics></math> time per window,
computing LogSTOP for <math id="S3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> over a sequence of length <math id="S3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="S3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)</annotation></semantics></math> time.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>LogSTOP for Query Matching</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define query matching with temporal properties as the task of predicting whether a given temporal property / query matches, or is expressed by, a sequence.
LogSTOPs can be used for matching sequence <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with query <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> by comparing <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}(X,\varphi,1,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}(X,\varphi,1,T)</annotation></semantics></math> with an appropriate threshold.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A natural first choice for such a threshold for LogSTOP is the constant <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\log 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\log 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. This threshold, is employed by existing works to determine if a video satisfies a temporal property <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. This, however, does not scale with the length of the sequence. For instance, given a 6-frame video with constant <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log 0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log 0.9</annotation></semantics></math> scores for "car",
the LogSTOP for temporal property "Always car", with <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=1</annotation></semantics></math>, is <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(0.9^{6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>0.9</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(0.9^{6})</annotation></semantics></math>. This is greater than <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(0.5)</annotation></semantics></math> and hence the video matches the query.
However, when another frame with the same high score <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(0.9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(0.9)</annotation></semantics></math> is added,
the score drops to <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(0.9^{7})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>0.9</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(0.9^{7})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is less than <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(0.5)</annotation></semantics></math> and hence the video no longer matches the query.
We would ideally also like the latter to match the query since the property "car" is detected with high scores.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We propose an adaptive threshold <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for query <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> and sequence length <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0.5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\hat{y}(\cdot,\varphi,1,T,w)\text{ using }\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,c,t)=\log 0.5\text{ for all }c\in C,1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> using </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0.5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\hat{y}(\cdot,\varphi,1,T,w)\text{ using }\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,c,t)=\log 0.5\text{ for all }c\in C,1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau(\varphi,T,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau(\varphi,T,w)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left\{\log 0.5,\,\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0.5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left\{\log 0.5,\,\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Informally, a sequence expresses a temporal property if the LogSTOP is higher than both random chance <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>
and LogSTOP using random chance predictors for local properties <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0.5</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{0.5}(\cdot,\varphi,T,w)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This threshold can be computed in <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T\cdot|\varphi|)</annotation></semantics></math> and is guaranteed to match at least as many sequences as the constant <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log 0.5</annotation></semantics></math> threshold.
For properties where the score decreases with sequence length (e.g., <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>), the adaptive threshold
allows more sequences to match
the query
than the constant threshold.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> LogSTOP for Ranked Sequence Retrieval</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Database </span><math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒟</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{X_{1},X_{2},\ldots,X_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, temporal property </span><math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, event length range </span><math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T_{lo},T_{hi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">o</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T_{lo},T_{hi})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, number of retrievals </span><math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">, smoothing window for LogSTOP </span><math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.800em">w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Ranked list </span><math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">R</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">[</mo><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">for</span><span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mi mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg2.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="alg2.l4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">do</span><span id="alg2.l4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
</span>
